From 906a9e7a4c8da2be0d8b2ceb30f374ea76920f7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 10:38:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH v4 3/6] rust: usb: add persistent bulk queues

Build bounded bulk-IN and bulk-OUT queues from reusable URBs.
Preallocate every slot and its DMA buffer at open, so a streaming
driver does not allocate on the transfer path, and require an I/O
token from the same interface for each operation.

Every queue URB is registered with the I/O window it was opened
against. Closing the window kills them, which releases anything blocked
waiting on a transfer, before the close waits for the last token to
drop; without that a driver blocked in recv() would keep the window
open across a suspend or a disconnect.

This lets streaming drivers reuse the common USB abstraction instead of
carrying private URB allocation, completion, cancellation and teardown
code.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
---
